WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.330
Allow me to tell you the classic children's
story of Chicken Little, otherwise known as

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.400
Henny Penny.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.270
As the tale goes, little Henny was outside
one day when an acorn fell from a tree and

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:15.770
hit her on the head.

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:20.151
Because of her naiveté and simple mindedness,
Henny foolishly began to believe the itself

00:00:20.151 --> 00:00:23.289
sky was falling down around her.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:28.190
She spent the rest of the day trying to convince
others, like Goosey Loosey and Turkey Lurkey,

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:32.570
that the sky was most certainly falling and
the world was surely coming to an end.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:37.340
In most versions of the story, the trip doesn't
end well for Henny and her hysterical friends

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.460
after they meet the sly Foxy Loxy.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.590
I don't want to give everything away, though,
so either read the story for yourself or check

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:49.620
out the classic season 6 episode of The Golden
Girls in which they reenact the tale.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:54.329
I mention Henny and Loosey and Turkey and
Foxy not just because they're great names

00:00:54.329 --> 00:00:59.690
to say, because it seems that just about everyone
is telling us the sky is falling these days.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:04.000
Between Trump, Russia, and North Korea, we've
got about half the country that is in total

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.469
freakout mode.

00:01:05.469 --> 00:01:08.630
Every day this freakout takes on a new urgency.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:11.979
One day the world is ending because America
left the Paris climate accord, another day

00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:16.710
it's because of net neutrality's reversal,
and another day it's because Trump holds his

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:18.880
water glass with two hands.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:23.220
This endless hysteria is not only being amplified
by the media, but it's actually being poked

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.240
and prodded by them as well.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:29.721
Blue check verified journalists on Twitter
who work for news organizations which are

00:01:29.721 --> 00:01:33.990
really nothing more than partisan activist
outlets want you to keep clicking on their

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:38.479
articles and videos, and they know the best
way to do that is to convince you that not

00:01:38.479 --> 00:01:42.690
only is the sky falling, but it's gonna land
directly on your head.

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:48.420
What if...just hear me out on this one...this
outrage factory is completely wrong and the

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.220
world isn't coming to an end just yet?

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:55.479
Crazy, I know, but I think it might just be
true.

00:01:55.479 --> 00:02:00.259
This doesn't mean things are perfect, but
but they are pretty damn good.

00:02:00.259 --> 00:02:05.270
This is the position of my guest this week,
Harvard psychology professor Steven Pinker.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:11.370
Pinker argues despite our world of perceived
horror and chaos, people are living longer,

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:17.629
healthier, happier, and freer lives right
now more than any other time in human history.

00:02:17.629 --> 00:02:21.540
This doesn't mean we don't have to work to
do, but if we don't stop and smell the roses

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:27.269
we might toss away all the goodness humans
have created for the prospect of a utopia

00:02:27.269 --> 00:02:28.879
that will never appear.

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:31.629
This is why I'm so proud of the work we've
done here on The Rubin Report.

00:02:31.629 --> 00:02:36.010
I really believe the conversations we're having
are at least some part of the antidote to

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:37.689
the craziness right now.

00:02:37.689 --> 00:02:41.629
If those of us who care about enlightenment
principles like science, reason and natural

00:02:41.629 --> 00:02:46.590
rights can make our voices louder then this
cliff we seem to be about to go off of might

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:50.010
just turn into a bridge to a better world..

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:55.059
Henny Penny's story took a drastic turn when
she met Foxy Loxy who tricked her and her

00:02:55.059 --> 00:02:57.150
friends to go to his lair.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:01.239
Well in real life we've got Wolf Blitzer in
a Situation Room.

00:03:01.239 --> 00:03:06.870
If the sky is falling maybe just changing
the channel is all you have to do to survive

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:07.010
the day...

